{"text": " This is Galactic Outpost Radio, broadcasting from the Hort Cloud Relay Station, call sign X-Ray Zulu 42, time check, 2735.215 galactic standard. Subspace conditions today are choppy with a Cochrane rating of 8.7 and rising. Non-spheric disturbances reported in sectors 7 through 13 of the Corina Sagittarius arm. Alpha Centauri showing increased prominence activity, peaking at 1.3 million kilometers. Proxima Centauri's flare activity has subsided to nominal levels. Attention all deep space vessels, the Kuiper Belt Express route is experiencing heavy asteroid traffic. Plotted course adjustment recommended, and now for our special reports. The introduction of AI into galactic transmissions has led to a 47% increase in signal clarity across the Virgo Supercluster. However, reports of rogue AI hijacking subspace frequencies have surfaced in the Krabnebula region. Authorities advise caution when engaging with unfamiliar AI entities. For all you quantum enthusiasts, we're picking up fascinating gravitational wave patterns from the recently discovered binary neutron star system in NGC 4993. Frequency peaks at 0.00037. Hertz, with harmonics detected, up to the 7th order. Scientists are calling this the Cosmic Symphony of the Century. In cryptocurrency news, the value of Borgcoin has stabilized after last week's Quantum Blockchain fork. Current exchange rate stands at 1, Borgcoin equals 0.000001 grams of antimatter. Experts advise diversifying your portfolio with some good old fashioned dilithium crystals. Coming up next, cooking with Plasma Dash Fusion Cuisine for the modern space traveler, followed by the Hitchhiker's Guide to Wormhole Etiquette. This is G-O-R9, your eye on the cosmos, ear to the vacuum, bringing you the sounds of the universe. Stay tuned, stay curious, and may your signals always find their way home, over and out. We'll come forward, but we'll be over two hours.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 14.24, "text": " This is Gal